# SPA fallback for hosts that support rewrite rules — Netlify and Cloudflare Pages.
#
# THIS FILE DOES NOTHING ON THE CURRENT DEPLOY. `.github/workflows/deploy.yml` publishes to
# GitHub Pages, which is a plain static file server: it has no rewrite rules and ignores this
# file entirely. Pages resolves /planner by looking for dist/planner/index.html, and serves
# /404.html when there is no file.
#
# That is why `scripts/prerender-og.mjs` writes a real index.html for every static route plus a
# 404.html catch-all, and why `stacking.test.ts` asserts the router and the prerender agree.
# Before this was noticed, /items, /planner, /stats, /reference and /survivors all returned
# GitHub's own 404 on refresh or on any shared link — including every URL the planner's
# "Copy link" button produces (§3j.147). It was invisible locally because `vite dev` and
# `vite preview` both provide the SPA fallback this file describes.
#
# Kept so the project stays portable to a host where it is the right mechanism.
/*    /index.html   200
